/* When tables next to code is off, the proc that splitAtProcPoints makes for
 * the call continuation after the stack check (a call to stg_gc_noregs) is
 * labelled with the label of its entry block. The x86 native code generator
 * used to print that label twice, and with -g the label that ends the proc
 * twice as well. GNU as rejects the second ("symbol `.LcN_proc_end' is
 * already defined") and so does clang for the first.
 */
bar (bits64 x)
{
  STK_CHK_GEN_N (16);
  return (x);
}
